{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":504426,"name":"","username":"Mitra","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a3d4f5/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T22:57:09.810Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Sept. 23, I created and trained 12 Grok Bots as a publishing company. I let the bots train that night after finishing setup.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe whole time, weekly usage showed 0% used. I thought the Grok Bot Galaxy / promotional allowance was unlimited for a period of time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe next morning I could not talk to them. The app said I needed a membership. I did not know the meter can sit at 0% while work is still using the grant.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI signed into another account in the same app, and when I switched back, all 12 publishing company bots were gone. Recover Grok Bot’s Computer failed: “The recovery couldn’t finish… Your Bots, files, and logins are safe.” I logged out and back in, thinking it was a bug, and hit a paywall. I can open the account again now, but the company bots are still missing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen usage or a plan runs out, Bots are supposed to go silent, not disappear. Imagine if I spend months building a company on these Bots and they can vanish after one night of training plus a logout. This makes it unreliable and doesn’t make sense to me.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI emailed cursor support to please check whether the missing Bots still exist or were deleted and explain why this login lost Grok Bot access while the usage showed 0% the whole time.\u003cbr\u003e\nSam said bots are stored separately from the computer, a used-up trial should not delete them, and a teammate would look (25 Sep). I did the checks he had recommended (listed below), but nothing worked. No further reply in 5 days.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSettings → General shows this same account on this device.\u003cbr\u003e\nI fully quit Grok Bot and reopened.\u003cbr\u003e\nThere is no Hidden Bots / Show hidden chats row at the bottom of the sidebar.\u003cbr\u003e\nAfter that I still only see dr eggbot and Chief of Staff. The publishing bots from 23 September are still missing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor cursor system bot: This is not billing. I am not asking about a plan, a refund, or a subscription, please keep this thread as a Bug Report so the Grok Bot team can see it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen Grok Bot on an account that has the Grok Bot Galaxy promotional credit\u003cbr\u003e\nCreate Grok Bots and train them, including an overnight run .\u003cbr\u003e\nWatch weekly usage. In this case it stayed at 0% used the whole time, even while the bots were working.\u003cbr\u003e\nNext morning the bots will not accept messages.\u003cbr\u003e\nAdd a second account in the same Grok Bot app, then switch back to the original account. The publishing roster is gone from the sidebar.\u003cbr\u003e\nRecover Grok Bot’s Computer fails (“bots, files, and logins are safe”).\u003cbr\u003e\nLog out and back in.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe company bots are still missing.\u003cbr\u003e\nConfirm Settings account, fully quit and reopen, check Hidden Bots. Still only two bots. Computer unreachable. Conversations will not load.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Grok Bot Galaxy promotional credit should show real usage while it is being spent, not stay stuck at 0%. When that credit runs out, the bots should stay on the account and only stop answering, with a clear “you need a plan” message.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdding a second login in the same app should not remove the first account’s roster. After quit and reopen, I should still see the same publishing company as on 23 Sep.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the grant is gone, I should be able to see the bots and understand that I need to pay to talk to them. They should not vanish. Support should be able to confirm the 23 Sep profiles still exist on this account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/5/7/5721a80633e2e6585e3212918a7b5ea6813d7051.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/cqNEc7AWAbDq8nYfB99IHPFXV5v.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-23 180109.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/5/7/5721a80633e2e6585e3212918a7b5ea6813d7051_2_207x500.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-23 180109.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"cqNEc7AWAbDq8nYfB99IHPFXV5v\" width=\"207\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/5/7/5721a80633e2e6585e3212918a7b5ea6813d7051_2_207x500.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/5/7/5721a80633e2e6585e3212918a7b5ea6813d7051_2_310x750.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/5/7/5721a80633e2e6585e3212918a7b5ea6813d7051.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"E5E4E4\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-23 180109.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e397×957 109 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/1/a/1a0fc7e9bc274e8690749d1bf9b59cfa06d85e2d.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/3IydVEzMOst9VaNtGWFrIOM4n6Z.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-25 211325.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/a/1a0fc7e9bc274e8690749d1bf9b59cfa06d85e2d_2_690x408.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-25 211325.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"3IydVEzMOst9VaNtGWFrIOM4n6Z\" width=\"690\" height=\"408\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/a/1a0fc7e9bc274e8690749d1bf9b59cfa06d85e2d_2_690x408.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/a/1a0fc7e9bc274e8690749d1bf9b59cfa06d85e2d_2_1035x612.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/a/1a0fc7e9bc274e8690749d1bf9b59cfa06d85e2d_2_1380x816.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"6C6C6C\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-25 211325.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e2559×1516 150 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-operating-system-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-operating-system-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-version-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-version-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion: 0.63.0\u003cbr\u003e\nBuilt: 2026-09-29T18:02:52.014Z\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: win32\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnknown. Grok Bot desktop agents. Conversations will not load so I cannot read a model name from a message.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504426-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504426-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T22:57:17.441Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":9,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":45.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173460,"topic_slug":"grok-bots-missing","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":140427,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bots-missing/173460/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":504458,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T23:40:56.511Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/mitra\"\u003e@Mitra\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the report, and sorry for the slow follow-up on your email.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGood news first: your 12 publishing Bots have not been deleted. They are still on your account. They’re hidden right now because the account no longer has active Grok Bot access, so the app can’t load them or reach Grok Bot’s computer. Signing into the second account didn’t remove them. It only cleared the list the app had saved on your device, and the app can’t reload that list without access.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbout the usage: the Grok Bot Galaxy credit is a fixed amount of free usage, not unlimited use for a period of time. Twelve Bots training at once used all of it by about 9:50 PM (Toronto time) on Sept 23. That credit is tracked separately from the Weekly Usage bar, which is why the bar stayed at 0% the whole time. I can see how that’s confusing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get your Bots back, the account needs Grok Bot access again. You can use Start Trial in the app, a paid plan that includes Grok Bot, or link a SuperGrok subscription. Once that’s active, fully quit and reopen Grok Bot with the same account, and your publishing Bots should show up again. Keep in mind that Bots working on their own overnight, or messaging each other, keep using usage the whole time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUntil then, please don’t use Recover Grok Bot’s Computer or Reset, and don’t recreate the Bots with the same names. If anything is still missing once access is back, reply here and we’ll take a look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T23:41:11.925Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":1,"readers_count":0,"score":0.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":173460,"topic_slug":"grok-bots-missing","display_username":"Kevin Neilson","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":105146,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bots-missing/173460/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[504426,504458]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":305,"name":"login","slug":"login"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bots missing","id":173460,"title":"Grok Bots missing","posts_count":2,"created_at":"2026-09-30T22:57:09.739Z","views":10,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-30T23:40:56.511Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"